  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - U.S. Technology for Energy Access and Minigrid Development, through SparkMeter, Inc</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant funds technical assistance (TA) to support energy access through solar minigrids and provide proof of concept for a U.S.-made digitalized system for minigrid management in Benin (Project). The Project is anticipated to generate new energy and provide energy access to thousands of people living in rural communities, creating greater social and economic inclusion and development. The grantee is Sherlock Grids SAS, and contractor is SparkMeter, Inc (Washington D.C.).</narrative>
  </description>
